<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sapienza University of Rome</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1303</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as La Sapienza</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sapienza University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> is a public university in Rome, founded in 1303 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-boniface-viii">Pope Boniface VIII</a> as a studium for the papal city. One of the largest universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, it is known for archaeology and Near Eastern studies; its mission under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paolo-matthiae">Paolo Matthiae</a> began excavating Tell Mardikh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1964 and identified the site as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> in 1968.</p></div>
